PROTOTYPE ONLY (ADR 0027 proposal, new windows on the Linux host, docs/proto-new-windows-ubuntu.md).
Never include this patch in a build used for a trial, the gate or a verdict;
scripts/build-compositor.sh does not know it.

A patch against gst-wayland-display (https://github.com/games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display,
MIT License), commit 1301f86. Apply the four measured patches in scripts/patches first, in order:
render-on-commit, cursor-messages, windows, dialogs; then, from scripts/patches/proto,
gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output.patch (U0), gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output-on-commit.patch
(step 1), and this one (step 2). The lines of context are from that project and those patches.

What it adds: the element with output=1 tells what its output shows. With its window-messages
property on, it posts the application message wayland.second-window on its bus: `present`, and
while a window is there its `title`, `width` and `height` (the second output's size in pixels) and
`key` (false in this step). It is posted when the element attaches, when the window is mapped on
the second output, when its title or the output's size changes (looked at on each commit of that
window), and when the window goes; never the same thing twice in a row. The compositor's side is a
sink (SecondWindowSink, Command::SecondWindowSink), as for the number of windows. The title is
never written into a log. With output=0 nothing changes: window-messages still posts
wayland.windows, the number of windows, which counts the second window as before.

scripts/proto-windows-ubuntu.py turns these messages into the list of other windows (a packet of
kind 6 of istesso-media) on the first window's connection. Three new compositor tests.

Not in it: input for the second window, popups, dialogs and resizing on the second output.

